WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
When you send on Aztec,

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.678
the private part of the work

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:04.174
happens on your computer,

00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:05.530
not on the network.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.165
Nulo runs it right here,

00:00:07.165 --> 00:00:09.217
with your keys and your notes.

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:11.409
Your keys, and what is in your notes,

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:13.287
stay on your computer.

00:00:13.287 --> 00:00:15.374
Then your computer builds a proof:

00:00:15.374 --> 00:00:16.939
math that shows this private

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:18.157
part follows the rules,

00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:19.896
without showing what is in it.

00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:21.461
The proof goes to the network,

00:00:21.461 --> 00:00:23.606
with sealed notes for the people you pay.

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:25.043
The network checks the proof,

00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:26.991
and if it holds, the transaction

00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:28.209
joins a block.

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:29.565
It never needed your private

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:30.678
data to trust it.

00:00:30.678 --> 00:00:32.835
Anything a transaction does in public,

00:00:32.835 --> 00:00:34.365
the network runs in the open,

00:00:34.365 --> 00:00:35.826
for everyone to see.

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:37.913
Later, one proof for a whole batch

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:39.930
of blocks is checked on Ethereum.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.878
Building a proof takes real work,

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:44.104
so it is the slow step before sending.
